// Title: PUA - NirCmd Execution As LOCAL SYSTEM
// Sigma ID: d9047477-0359-48c9-b8c7-792cedcdc9c4
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-01-24 | Modified: 2023-02-13
// ATT&CK: execution, T1569.002, S0029
// Description: Detects the use of NirCmd tool for command execution as SYSTEM user
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use by administrators
// References:
//   - https://www.nirsoft.net/utils/nircmd.html
//   - https://www.winhelponline.com/blog/run-program-as-system-localsystem-account-windows/
//   - https://www.nirsoft.net/utils/nircmd2.html#using
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pua_nircmd_as_system.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains " runassystem "
